https://www.scholarships.net.in/64823.html,"Organisation: Nehru Sidhant Kender TrustScholarship Name: Satya Scholarship Program 2026Applicable For: First year students in 3 to 5-year undergraduate or integrated master’s coursesLast Date: 30th July 2026Website:https://www.buddy4study.com/page/satya-scholarship-program

Table of Contents

Nehru Sidhant Kender Trust has launched the Satya Scholarship Program 2026, a merit-cum-means initiative designed to assist students from various socio-economic backgrounds in pursuing higher education after Class 12. The scholarship offers 100% coverage of annual course fees, plus accommodation and meal support, for students enrolled in 3–5-year undergraduate or integrated master’s programs in Commerce, Engineering & Technology, and Medical & Health Sciences. Last date of application is 30th July 2026.

1. Open to first-year students in 3 to 5-year undergraduate or integrated master’s courses in:** Commerce: BBA, B.Com** Engineering and Technology: B.Tech, B.E. (all streams), B.Sc. (Engineering), BCA, B.Arch** Medical and Health Sciences: MBBS, BDS, BPT, B.Sc. (Nursing), B.Sc. (Allied and Healthcare)

2. Must have passed Class 12 Board Exam from a recognised board in Punjab with at least 60% aggregate.3. Students from Punjab at 38 selected institutes in Ludhiana or Top 50 NIRF-ranked institutions in India are eligible. (Please refer to the eligible college list)4. Annual parental income must not exceed INR 8 lakh; guardian income limits apply for orphans.5. Applicants must be Indian citizens and not recipients of any other educational scholarship.

** 100% of the annual course fee coverage as per the approved fee structure of the selected institute, for the full duration of the course (3 to 5 years).** Hostel and mess charges or PG/rented accommodation support will be provided to all eligible scholars studying outside their hometown, based on the institute’s approved charges or actual expenses incurred, whichever is lower.** For institutes without hostel facilities, a fixed monthly stipend of ₹5,000 will be provided towards accommodation and meals.

To apply for Satya Scholarship Program, Follow the below steps

Steps:** Go to the link given above and Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button.** Login to Buddy4Study with your registered ID and land on the ‘Application Form Page’.** If not registered, sign up on Buddy4Study using email, mobile, or Gmail.** You will now be redirected to the ‘Satya Scholarship Program 2026′ application form page.** Click on ‘Start Application’ to begin.** Fill in the required details.** Upload relevant documents.** Accept the ‘Terms and Conditions’ and click ‘Preview’.** If all details are correct, click the ‘Submit’ button to complete the process.

1. Recent passport-sized photograph2. Proof of identity (Masked Aadhaar, Driving License, Voter ID Card, PAN Card or any government-approved ID)3. Current-year admission letter issued by the institute4. Class XII marksheet5. Institute fee structure6. Bank account details of the student and the parent/guardian7. Crisis-related documents, such as a parent’s death certificate or proof of critical illness (if applicable)8. PwD certificate or sports achievement certificates, if applicable9. Statement of Purpose (SOP) outlining the applicant’s aspirations and reasons for applying for the scholarship10. Parental Income Proof

Last Date of Nehru Sidhant Kender Trust Satya Scholarship Program is 30th July 2026.Author : Jency

