The Raman Kant Munjal Scholarship for 2026-27, initiated by the Raman Kant Munjal Foundation and supported by Hero FinCorp, is designed to assist students in finance-related fields in achieving their career aspirations. This scholarship offers financial support of up to INR 5,50,000 per year for three years to students currently in their first year of various programs, including BBA, BFIA, B.Com (H, E), Bachelor of Management Studies (BMS), Integrated Program in Management (IPM), B.A. (Economics), and Bachelor in Business Studies (BBS), among other finance-related degrees. Last date of application is 31st August 2026.

** Open to students across India currently enrolled in the first year of BBA, BFIA, B.Com (H, E), Bachelor of Management Studies (BMS), Integrated Program in Management (IPM), B.A. (Economics), Bachelor in Business Studies (BBS), or any other finance-related degree course.** Applicants must have secured at least 80% marks in Classes 10 and 12 (For PwD students, the minimum percentage required is 70% marks).** The annual parental income of the applicant must not exceed INR 6 lakh from all sources.** Open for Indian nationals only.** The children of employees/contract employees of Hero FinCorp, Raman Kant Munjal Foundation, and Buddy4Study are ineligible to apply.

Scholarships ranging from INR 40,000 to INR 5,50,000 per year will be awarded to each scholar for three years to complete their education.

