https://www.scholarships.net.in/64856.html,"Organisation: Aakash FoundationScholarship Name: Aakash National Talent Hunt Exam (ANTHE) Scholarship 2026Applicable For: Class of VI, VII, VIII, IX, X, XI & XII StudentsPrizes: Win Upto 100%* Scholarship On Medical, Engineering & Foundation CoursesLast Date: 3 Days Before the Examination DateExam Dates: 03, 04, 10 & 11th October 2026Website:https://anthe.aakash.ac.in/anthe

Table of Contents

Aakash National Talent Hunt Exam (ANTHE) Scholarship 2026 is the India’s biggest scholarship exam. Students studying in Class VI, VII, VIII, IX, X, XI & XII can appear in the exam. Participate and win upto 100%* scholarship on Medical, Engineering & Foundation courses. Online exam will be held on 03, 04, 10 & 11th October 2026. Registration ends on 3 Days before the Examination Date.

Students studying in Class VI, VII, VIII, IX, X, XI & XII can appear in the Aakash National Talent Hunt Scholarship Exam.

Three simple steps to secure your spot at ANTHE 2026.

1. Verify mobile number:Enter your mobile number to receive a one-time password.

2. Submit your details:Fill in the short online form and submit your application.

3. Registration successful:Get your admit card and login details to start preparing.

Scholarships up to 100%. Every registered student is eligible for merit-based scholarships on their tuition and exam fees.

Frequently Asked Questions FAQ On Aakash National Talent Hunt Scholarship Exam

What is the exam pattern of ANTHE 2026?For Classes V–VI, the paper will have 40 questions for 80 marks. For Classes VII–XII, there will be 40 questions for 90 marks. The duration of the test is 1 hour with no negative marking. Visit anthe.aakash.ac.in/syllabus for the class-wise syllabus.

How and when will the exam be conducted?ANTHE 2026 will be held in both online and offline modes. The offline exam is scheduled on 3rd, 4th, 10th, and 11th October, while the online exam will be conducted every day from 3rd to 11th October.

How much scholarship can I get through ANTHE?Students appearing through Offline Mode can get up to 100% scholarship covering all applicable fee components. Students appearing through Online Mode can get up to 80% scholarship on Tuition Fees only.

How many times can a student change exam details?A student can change exam details up to two times. As per the Terms & Conditions, exam details can be changed up to 7 days before the examination for Offline Mode and up to 3 days before the examination for Online Mode.

Which courses can I get a scholarship on through ANTHE?ANTHE gives students a chance to get up to 100%* Scholarship on Medical (NEET), Engineering (JEE), and Foundation Classroom and Aakash Digital courses. ANTHE Scholarship is also valid on Aakash Invictus courses.

Can a student give the exam on a Mobile Phone or Tablet?Yes. Students can take the ANTHE exam on a mobile phone, tablet, laptop, or desktop computer, provided they have a stable internet connection and a supported web browser. For the best experience, using a laptop or desktop is recommended.

Are there any practice tests available for ANTHE preparation?Yes, one sample paper will be provided free of cost to every student and shall be available on the portal upon registration for ANTHE. Students who wish to practice for ANTHE 2026 may purchase 4 mock tests at INR 50, with 1 paper unlocked every month from June 2026 to September 2026.

How can a student change the class, stream, date, or mode of the exam?Log in to anthe.aakash.ac.in/login using your credentials and make the required changes.

What should we do if payment is deducted but registration is unsuccessful?If the payment is deducted but the registration is unsuccessful, please wait for up to 3 working days. If the payment is not credited back within this period, raise the issue by filling out the Google Form at https://forms.gle/NpDjEg3cCavVgZ118. Keep all transaction details and screenshots ready before submitting the form.

For Offline Mode, registration closes 7 days before the examination date. For Online Mode, registration closes 3 days before the examination date.Author : Jency

